select app.guide_release_section('va', 'academy', 'chapter', 'commissions', 'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**. There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.

## Watch the lessons

1. Open **Academy**. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.
2. Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser''s own voice.
3. Press **Play**. **Pause**, **Back** and **Next** move through the scenes; **Replay** starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. **Voice on** turns the voice off and on.
4. No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.

> Tip: Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser''s, so it can sound different on another device.

## Pass the quiz

1. Under the lessons, answer every question and press **Check my answers**.
2. You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press **Try again** as often as you need.
3. A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.

> Good to know: An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. The academy gate is on: each section opens once you pass the one before it. If you were hired with one-step Hire, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths (the guide and your profile stay open). Each path ends with a section on what changed recently.

## Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)

Your first sign-in opens **Welcome**, your onboarding checklist, in four steps:

1. Welcome.
2. Your profile and phone: add your home address and your mobile number in your profile.
3. The academy: pass every section of your path. Each quiz passes at 80%, and you can retake it as often as you need.
4. Your first tasks: press **Done** on each one as you finish it.

Until you pass the academy, Welcome, the academy, the guide and your profile are all that opens; any other page brings you back to Welcome. Then **Go to your portal** opens everything.

## Quiz rules (release 35)

A quiz passes at 90%. Questions come in a random order and open after the reading time. After a failed try, wait 30 minutes; you have 3 tries a day. New sections for your role are added to your path: if you had passed everything, you keep a week before they hold you, and nothing you passed is reset.

## The renter''s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)

Every staff role now has the path **The renter''s side**: one section for each step a renter takes (the request, the offer, Complete your details and signing, paying and the deposit hold, coverage proof with the pink slip and OPCF 27, pickup, the trip, the return and the deposit back, and the errors renters call about). Each step shows what the renter sees and opens that page of the renter guide (**Renter guide**, at `/staff/guide/renter`). Your own path also has a section of worked examples from your chapter of this guide: what the renter says, where you click and what you say.

1. New staff take both from the start, before their portal opens.
2. Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date. After it, the rest of the portal waits until the new sections are passed. Nothing you passed is reset.
3. **Ask the guide first**: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on, with a link. Read it before you ask a colleague, and say which chapter you read when you do.', 'Academy', 'Your training path: lessons narrated by your browser, a quiz per section, 80% to pass.',
  'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**. There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.

## Watch the lessons

1. Open **Academy**. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.
2. Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser''s own voice.
3. Press **Play**. **Pause**, **Back** and **Next** move through the scenes; **Replay** starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. **Voice on** turns the voice off and on.
4. No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.
5. Each section ends with a lesson called **See it**: pictures of the real screens with numbered pins, good and bad example photos side by side, flow diagrams and Do and Do not pairs. Press **Next** to go through them.

> Tip: Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser''s, so it can sound different on another device.

## Pass the quiz

1. Under the lessons, answer every question and press **Check my answers**. Every question also has one funny wrong answer among the options: picking it is simply wrong, and the line under it says so.
2. You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press **Try again** as often as you need.
3. A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.

> Good to know: An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. The academy gate is on: each section opens once you pass the one before it. If you were hired with one-step Hire, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths (the guide and your profile stay open). Each path ends with a section on what changed recently.

## Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)

Your first sign-in opens **Welcome**, your onboarding checklist, in four steps:

1. Welcome.
2. Your profile and phone: add your home address and your mobile number in your profile.
3. The academy: pass every section of your path. Each quiz passes at 80%, and you can retake it as often as you need.
4. Your first tasks: press **Done** on each one as you finish it.

Until you pass the academy, Welcome, the academy, the guide and your profile are all that opens; any other page brings you back to Welcome. Then **Go to your portal** opens everything.

## Quiz rules (release 35)

A quiz passes at 90%. Questions come in a random order and open after the reading time. After a failed try, wait 30 minutes; you have 3 tries a day. New sections for your role are added to your path: if you had passed everything, you keep a week before they hold you, and nothing you passed is reset.

## The renter''s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)

Every staff role now has the path **The renter''s side**: one section for each step a renter takes (the request, the offer, Complete your details and signing, paying and the deposit hold, coverage proof with the pink slip and OPCF 27, pickup, the trip, the return and the deposit back, and the errors renters call about). Each step shows what the renter sees and opens that page of the renter guide (**Renter guide**, at `/staff/guide/renter`). Your own path also has a section of worked examples from your chapter of this guide: what the renter says, where you click and what you say.

1. New staff take both from the start, before their portal opens.
2. Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date. After it, the rest of the portal waits until the new sections are passed. Nothing you passed is reset.
3. **Ask the guide first**: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on, with a link. Read it before you ask a colleague, and say which chapter you read when you do.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Your training path is under <b class="gd-ui">Me</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>. There is a path for each of your functions: customer service, fleet, finance, Sales in person or remote, field work.</p><section class="gd-task" id="academy-watch-the-lessons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Watch the lessons</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>. Each path lists its sections in order, with Passed, Open or Pass the one before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a section. Each lesson is a short video made by your browser: scenes with captions, read aloud by your browser&#39;s own voice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Play</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Back</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Next</b> move through the scenes; <b class="gd-ui">Replay</b> starts again; Speed goes from 0.75x to 1.5x. <b class="gd-ui">Voice on</b> turns the voice off and on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">No sound or no English voice on your device? The lesson plays with captions only, each scene timed for reading.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Each section ends with a lesson called <b class="gd-ui">See it</b>: pictures of the real screens with numbered pins, good and bad example photos side by side, flow diagrams and Do and Do not pairs. Press <b class="gd-ui">Next</b> to go through them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Use headphones in the office. The voice is your browser&#39;s, so it can sound different on another device.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-pass-the-quiz" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pass the quiz</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under the lessons, answer every question and press <b class="gd-ui">Check my answers</b>. Every question also has one funny wrong answer among the options: picking it is simply wrong, and the line under it says so.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">You need 80% (the pass mark in Program settings). Passed: the next section opens. Not yet: each answer shows the right one and why; press <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b> as often as you need.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A section that is on two of your paths (the policies, for example) counts on both once passed.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>An Admin can open a section early for you, for example when you already did this work somewhere else. The academy gate is on: each section opens once you pass the one before it. If you were hired with one-step Hire, the rest of the portal waits until you pass your paths (the guide and your profile stay open). Each path ends with a section on what changed recently.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-your-first-steps-welcome-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your first sign-in opens <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b>, your onboarding checklist, in four steps:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Welcome.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Your profile and phone: add your home address and your mobile number in your profile.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The academy: pass every section of your path. Each quiz passes at 80%, and you can retake it as often as you need.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Your first tasks: press <b class="gd-ui">Done</b> on each one as you finish it.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Until you pass the academy, Welcome, the academy, the guide and your profile are all that opens; any other page brings you back to Welcome. Then <b class="gd-ui">Go to your portal</b> opens everything.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-quiz-rules-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Quiz rules (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">A quiz passes at 90%. Questions come in a random order and open after the reading time. After a failed try, wait 30 minutes; you have 3 tries a day. New sections for your role are added to your path: if you had passed everything, you keep a week before they hold you, and nothing you passed is reset.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-renter-s-side-and-ask-the-guide-first-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The renter&#39;s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every staff role now has the path <b class="gd-ui">The renter&#39;s side</b>: one section for each step a renter takes (the request, the offer, Complete your details and signing, paying and the deposit hold, coverage proof with the pink slip and OPCF 27, pickup, the trip, the return and the deposit back, and the errors renters call about). Each step shows what the renter sees and opens that page of the renter guide (<b class="gd-ui">Renter guide</b>, at <span class="gd-url">/staff/guide/renter</span>). Your own path also has a section of worked examples from your chapter of this guide: what the renter says, where you click and what you say.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">New staff take both from the start, before their portal opens.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date. After it, the rest of the portal waits until the new sections are passed. Nothing you passed is reset.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Ask the guide first</b>: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on, with a link. Read it before you ask a colleague, and say which chapter you read when you do.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'academy', 'chapter', 'my-hours-and-pay', 'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**: the handover, the return, cash and signing in the field, and the rules of the trip.

1. Open **Academy** and the first open section.
2. Press **Play** on each lesson: scenes with captions, read aloud by your phone''s own voice. **Pause**, **Back**, **Next**, **Replay** and Speed work as on a video. No voice on your phone? The captions play by themselves.
3. Answer the quiz and press **Check my answers**. 80% passes and opens the next section; **Try again** as often as you need. Until you pass your path, the rest of the portal waits (the guide and your profile stay open).

> Tip: Nothing is downloaded: the lessons work on mobile data and use very little of it.

## Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)

Your first sign-in opens **Welcome**: welcome, then your profile and phone, then the academy, then your first tasks (press **Done** on each). Until you pass the academy, only Welcome, the academy, the guide and your profile open.

## Quiz rules (release 35)

A quiz passes at 90%, opens after the reading time, waits 30 minutes after a failed try and allows 3 tries a day. You get field jobs only once you have passed and hold a shift that day.

## The renter''s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)

Your training now has the path **The renter''s side**: what the renter sees at each step, from the request to the deposit back, with each page of the renter guide (**Renter guide**, at `/staff/guide/renter`). Your field path also has a section of worked examples from this guide: the ready check, the original licence, cash and add-ons.

1. New staff take both from the start. Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date; after it, the rest of the portal waits until they are passed.
2. **Ask the guide first**: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on. Read it before you call the office.', 'Academy', 'Your training: watch the lessons on your phone, pass each quiz.',
  'Your training path is under **Me** > **Academy**: the handover, the return, cash and signing in the field, and the rules of the trip.

1. Open **Academy** and the first open section.
2. Press **Play** on each lesson: scenes with captions, read aloud by your phone''s own voice. **Pause**, **Back**, **Next**, **Replay** and Speed work as on a video. No voice on your phone? The captions play by themselves. Each section ends with a lesson called **See it**: pictures of the real screens with numbered pins, good and bad example photos, flow diagrams and Do and Do not pairs.
3. Answer the quiz and press **Check my answers**. Every question has one funny wrong answer among the options: picking it is simply wrong. 80% passes and opens the next section; **Try again** as often as you need. Until you pass your path, the rest of the portal waits (the guide and your profile stay open).

> Tip: Nothing is downloaded: the lessons work on mobile data and use very little of it.

## Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)

Your first sign-in opens **Welcome**: welcome, then your profile and phone, then the academy, then your first tasks (press **Done** on each). Until you pass the academy, only Welcome, the academy, the guide and your profile open.

## Quiz rules (release 35)

A quiz passes at 90%, opens after the reading time, waits 30 minutes after a failed try and allows 3 tries a day. You get field jobs only once you have passed and hold a shift that day.

## The renter''s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)

Your training now has the path **The renter''s side**: what the renter sees at each step, from the request to the deposit back, with each page of the renter guide (**Renter guide**, at `/staff/guide/renter`). Your field path also has a section of worked examples from this guide: the ready check, the original licence, cash and add-ons.

1. New staff take both from the start. Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date; after it, the rest of the portal waits until they are passed.
2. **Ask the guide first**: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on. Read it before you call the office.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Your training path is under <b class="gd-ui">Me</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>: the handover, the return, cash and signing in the field, and the rules of the trip.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b> and the first open section.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Play</b> on each lesson: scenes with captions, read aloud by your phone&#39;s own voice. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Back</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Next</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Replay</b> and Speed work as on a video. No voice on your phone? The captions play by themselves. Each section ends with a lesson called <b class="gd-ui">See it</b>: pictures of the real screens with numbered pins, good and bad example photos, flow diagrams and Do and Do not pairs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Answer the quiz and press <b class="gd-ui">Check my answers</b>. Every question has one funny wrong answer among the options: picking it is simply wrong. 80% passes and opens the next section; <b class="gd-ui">Try again</b> as often as you need. Until you pass your path, the rest of the portal waits (the guide and your profile stay open).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Nothing is downloaded: the lessons work on mobile data and use very little of it.</div></aside><section class="gd-task" id="academy-your-first-steps-welcome-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your first steps: Welcome (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your first sign-in opens <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b>: welcome, then your profile and phone, then the academy, then your first tasks (press <b class="gd-ui">Done</b> on each). Until you pass the academy, only Welcome, the academy, the guide and your profile open.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-quiz-rules-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Quiz rules (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">A quiz passes at 90%, opens after the reading time, waits 30 minutes after a failed try and allows 3 tries a day. You get field jobs only once you have passed and hold a shift that day.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-renter-s-side-and-ask-the-guide-first-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The renter&#39;s side and Ask the guide first (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your training now has the path <b class="gd-ui">The renter&#39;s side</b>: what the renter sees at each step, from the request to the deposit back, with each page of the renter guide (<b class="gd-ui">Renter guide</b>, at <span class="gd-url">/staff/guide/renter</span>). Your field path also has a section of worked examples from this guide: the ready check, the original licence, cash and add-ons.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">New staff take both from the start. Staff already working have 7 days: the academy page says the date; after it, the rest of the portal waits until they are passed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Ask the guide first</b>: the Assistant panel names the guide chapter of the page you are on. Read it before you call the office.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
